nslation my  father was deeply indebted to his fans  to their loyalty and always hoped his  work would pass through to following  generations that they're renewing it is  the only thing that they're saying at  this time there's no details about when  we should expect to see more episodes  when they're gonna start filming or  anything along those lines in the ama  when he was asked about it he said that  they have a vague release schedule but  because of the uncertainties of kobit we  would never announce a release date  until a given season had finished  filming he had several questions asking  if they thought they could improve  things and he said yes i would love to  improve on a host of things and i think  you will see with season two that we  already have the first thing we did from  soup to nuts is say what can we improve  on and when asked about hints he says  hobermallow bel rios a strong general  and a weak emperor and the church of the  galactic spirit he mentioned the  characters hobermallow and general bel  rios in the articles and we also heard  gail mention those names in the opening  of the first episode as far as the  timeline and how much of the story  they're telling before the show ever  came out he pitched it as an eight  season plan and they talked about how  this was a story that was a thousand  years long this brought up some  questions for people who had read the  series because the timeline in the books  only makes it about 500 years past the  beginning of the foundation of course  the setup is that establishing the  foundation will shorten the inner regnum  that 30 000 years of barbarism that was  supposed to come after the empire falls  their plan is supposed to shorten that  time frame down to a thousand years  until a new empire can take its place so  when he was asked about the show's  timeline he said that if we're able to  do the full eight season plan we will  eventually progress beyond the 500 plus  fe that azimov got to in his novels that  was always anticipated with the asimov  estate so 500 plus fe relates to the  timeline the first year of the  foundation became year number one fe and  the stories he wrote went about 500  years beyond that  some fans brought up questions about  what books they're actually adapting  what they had rights to goyer's answer  was we have rights to all the foundation  books just not the others and here when  he says the others he's talking about  the empire series and the robot series  asimov connected those all together at  the end but they're not bundled as the  same intellectual property this was a  question if they had rights to all the  foundation books rather than just the  trilogy and since they're connected  would that also include concepts from  the robot series as you've seen with  demarzo on the show robots have a long  life span compared to humans so this  character is present in both series and  takes on different names at different  points of the story goyer used this to  explain some of the rights issues  between the series saying our danielle  oliva is part of the irobot's rights  which skydance  apple do not have access to we have  access to the demerseal side of the  character if that makes sense so there's  a shared history which it sounds like  the show can draw from but they just  can't use the name this confirmed who  the character was since some book  readers were questioning that but it  also brought up some questions about  things we've seen happen in relation to  the laws of robotics he said that  asimov's robotics laws do exist in the  universe of the show but that doesn't  necessarily mean that demarzel is  presently bound by them and to explain  further would spoil far too much so a  user named argentis asked this question  how do you have rights to the laws of  robotics but not demarzel's book  identity they seem congruent he said we  were given a clear dictate as to what  rights we have access to what rights are  shared and which ones are off limits so  just to bring all that together they do  have the rights to adapt all seven books  in the foundation series the two  prequels where asimov went back and gave  harry selden a backstory fleshed out  some of the details about how he put  psycho history together on trantor the  original trilogy and the two books that  came after that where asimov was trying  to bring the story to an end he never  actually did that though the final book  foundation and earth doesn't have a  definitive ending the story in the book  ends but to say it in a spoiler-free way  there are a lot of questions about how  things will proceed from there that  brings things back to him saying that  they would go beyond the 500 plus years  in the books and the idea of a thousand  year tale he touched on that saying gaia  slash galaxia is a possibility but i  also have inside info on how asimov was  thinking of ending the thing so if we  get there we'll be exploring that just  to be clear asimov planned on writing  another book beyond foundation and earth  he was having trouble working it all out  and that's when he decided to add the  prequels and then he died not long after  he finished writing them the implication  here is that the show is setting out to  complete the story if and it's a big if  in today's television climate they get  to make eight seasons in relation to  changes they made for the adaptation he  pointed out it was a remix of the story  and said season one loosely adapts  stories from the first book while  weaving in some characters and concepts  from the prequels for those who read the  books as surmised the number of the  show's characters are composite  characters gale is a combo of two  characters the other of which book  readers may well guess cleon the 14th  also has elements of leopold the first  etc and about the characterization of  salvor hardin which there were a lot of  questions about he said our salvor is  not the fully formed salver of the books  